  "scientific_acceptance": [
    "For every finite paired Boolean input, including empty input, the actual step relation reaches its first halt after exactly 5*n+2 transitions. RunsToHalt excludes padded halt steps.",
    "Four forward transitions per cell load the source bit, XOR the destination, clear scratch, and advance. Rewind traverses n cells; two boundary observations enter rewind and halt. No executed transition uses unbounded Nat arithmetic or an external length counter.",
    "The output target decodes to unsigned Nat XOR, source bits are unchanged, head returns to the left boundary and the initially clean one-bit scratch is clean again.",
    "The paired tape cell count is conserved for arbitrary states, including malformed control states. This means n cells plus constant scratch/control, not constant total tape space.",
    "Two scans restore the pair list using an explicit external halt-to-load reset. The theorem does not include that reset or initial paired layout construction in the per-scan count."
  ],
  "limits_and_remaining": [
    "Boundary observation is primitive in the declared bounded-zipper model. A conventional single-symbol tape/marked-alphabet lowering requires a separate simulation and may have a different exact count.",
    "The paired same-width layout, end-marker interpretation and initialization costs remain supplied; arbitrary dirty scratch restoration is not claimed.",
    "Cell representation/alignment, selected physical allocation/executor refinement, all-size multiplication and total bit-complexity are not discharged."
  ],
